<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<loadFolders>
  <v1.6>
    <li>/</li>
    <!-- Once a LoadFolders.xml exists, ONLY the folders listed here load - the
         game's default roots (version folder, Common, /) no longer apply. Common/
         is documented in CLAUDE.md as the home for version-independent assets, so
         it must be listed or its Languages/Textures silently never load. -->
    <li>Common</li>
    <li>1.6</li>
    <!-- Optional-mod/DLC compat roots, one gated entry each (the layout the wider
         ecosystem uses). Needed whenever content can't gate itself: defs support
         MayRequire, but DefInjected entries do not (the loader ignores attributes
         on them) and textures have no node to carry one at all, so the load root
         *is* the gate. Gating is by package id via IfModActive (LoadFolders knows
         nothing about MayRequire, and unlike PatchOperationFindMod it matches the
         package id rather than the display name).

         Two roots per optional mod, mirroring how the ungated roots above split:
         Mods/<Mod Name>/ for version-independent content (art) and
         1.6/Mods/<Mod Name>/ for version-specific content (Defs, and the
         DefInjected that must sit in the same load root as the defs it targets).
         Both are safe to nest, because the game only scans well-known folders
         (Languages/, Defs/, Textures/, ...) directly under a load root - so the
         plain "/", Common and 1.6 entries above never see Mods/. ModLister also
         scans the game's Mods folder one level deep only, so a nested Mods/
         inside a deployed mod is never mistaken for a mod.

         Odyssey is this mod's planned optional gate (the set targets Odyssey's
         end-game content but must not require the DLC). Uncomment when the first
         Odyssey-only def, injection or texture lands:
    <li IfModActive="ludeon.rimworld.odyssey">Mods/Odyssey</li>
    <li IfModActive="ludeon.rimworld.odyssey">1.6/Mods/Odyssey</li>
    -->
  </v1.6>
</loadFolders>
